        "original_id": "9a994581-1d0f-5eef-b468-c61622bb6b14",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hudson Austin, Maurice Bishop, Eric Gairy\n- Organizations: New Jewel Movement\n- Places: Grenada\n- Roles: chairman, politician, leader\n- Events: 13 March 1979 revolution, killing of Maurice Bishop\n- Concepts: socio-economic development, education, Black liberation\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1979, the New Jewel Movement came to power in Grenada during a revolution that removed Eric Gairy from office.\n- Maurice Rupert Bishop was born on 29 May 1944 and died on 19 October 1983.\n- Maurice Bishop was a Grenadian politician and the leader of the New Jewel Movement.\n- The New Jewel Movement promoted popular efforts in socio-economic development, education, and Black liberation.\n- After the killing of Maurice Bishop, Hudson Austin formed a military government in Grenada and ruled it as chairman.",
